==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|roialté}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈɹɔɪəlti/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-royalty.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|royalties}}

# The [[rank]], [[status]], [[power]] or [[authority]] of a monarch.
# People of [[royal]] [[rank]], plus their [[families]], treated as a [[group]].
# A royal [[right]] or [[prerogative]], such as the [[exploitation]] of a [[natural resource]]; the [[granting]] of such a right; [[payment]] received for such a right.
# The payment received by an owner of real property for exploitation of [[mineral right]]s on his property.
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Payment made to a [[writer]], [[composer]], [[inventor]] etc for the [[sale]] or [[use]] of [[intellectual property]], [[invention]] etc.
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} Someone in a privileged position 
#* {{quote-journal|author=Daniel Taylor|title=England humiliated as Iceland knock them out of Euro 2016|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2016/jun/27/england-iceland-euro-2016-match-report|newspaper={{w|The Guardian}}|city=London|date=27 June 2016|passage=England will have another manager for the next World Cup, Hodgson’s reign will be defined by a result comparable to losing to the United States in the 1950 World Cup and the now-familiar inquest will begin again in a country that likes to see itself as football '''royalty'''.}}
# {{lb|en|poker|slang}} A [[king]] and a [[queen]] as a starting hand in [[Texas hold 'em]].

